    "finding_summary": "The checkout-api service is experiencing SEV2 latency after deploying v2.19.0 with a new retry feature flag defaulted on 11 minutes before symptom onset. Current signal shows p95 latency exceeding 3000ms with 8x error budget burn rate. Log evidence confirms retry attempts per request increased from 1 to 5, causing queue depth to increase. Upstream payment gateway health is normal, ruling out dependency outage. A prior incident (INC-2025-144) involved the same retry feature causing similar request amplification and latency. The Bad Deploy Runbook applies when symptoms begin shortly after a service deploy and dependency health is normal, which matches this scenario.",
